  "final_response": "By Legendre’s formula, $v_2\\binom{2n}{n} = \\sum_{i=1}^\\infty \\left( \\left\\lfloor \\frac{2n}{2^i} \\right\\rfloor - 2\\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{2^i} \\right\\rfloor \\right) = s_2(n)$, as each term counts the carry in binary addition $n+n$, and total carries equal number of 1s in $n$. Then $v_2(C_n) = v_2\\binom{2n}{n} - v_2(n+1) = s_2(n) - v_2(n+1)$. For $C_n$ odd, require $s_2(n) = v_2(n+1)$. This occurs iff $n = 2^k - 1$, since then binary of $n$ is $k$ ones ($s_2(n)=k$), and $n+1=2^k$ ($v_2(n+1)=k$). Thus $C_n$ is odd exactly when $n$ is one less than a power of two.",
